Alice, Carol,

I finished the benchmark results for the new endpoints. Summary:

  Endpoint              | p50   | p95   | p99
  ----------------------|-------|-------|------
  POST /v2/users        | 12ms  | 45ms  | 120ms
  GET  /v2/users/:id    | 3ms   | 8ms   | 22ms
  PUT  /v2/users/:id    | 15ms  | 52ms  | 145ms
  DELETE /v2/users/:id  | 5ms   | 12ms  | 35ms
  POST /v2/users/bulk   | 85ms  | 340ms | 890ms
  GET  /v2/search       | 22ms  | 95ms  | 250ms

The bulk endpoint is about 30% faster than v1 thanks to the batched
writes. Search is slightly slower due to the new faceting logic but
still well within SLA.

I also ran a 10-minute stress test at 5x normal traffic. No errors,
memory stayed flat, CPU peaked at 62%. Looks solid.

- Bob

